96..104: `@export` cannot be applied to the generic function `exported`: it has one body per instantiation and so no single symbol to export; export a non-generic function that calls it at the types the host needs
131..135: the generic function `asks` with a `uses` clause is not supported by the code generator yet: effect evidence is passed to one body per function, and a generic function has one per instantiation
265..269: instantiating the generic functions `main` calls does not terminate: `grow` calls `grow` at an ever larger type (its type arguments nest more than 32 deep and keep growing), so there is no finite set of instances to generate
